# Trivy ignore file — R17.
#
# Add named CVE/finding IDs here ONLY when there is no upstream fix and the
# risk is formally accepted.  Each entry must include:
#   1. The finding ID (CVE-YYYY-NNNNN or Trivy check ID).
#   2. A dated comment with the reason and re-review date.
#   3. A reference issue / ticket where the deferral was approved.
#
# Example (do not uncomment without a real acceptance decision):
#   CVE-2024-12345  # python:3.12-slim base — no fix as of 2025-06-16; low
#                   # exploitability in containerised runtime; revisit 2025-09.
#                   # Tracked: https://github.com/org/resto/issues/NNN
#
# NEVER add entries without justification; never add wildcards or ecosystem-
# wide ignores.  The goal is zero entries here through timely patching.

# ── Deferred: brace-expansion OOM DoS — dev/build tooling only ────────────────
# Present only in the frontend build/lint/test toolchain (eslint, glob,
# minimatch, workbox-build, vitest js-beautify) — NEVER in the shipped bundle,
# and it only ever expands our own source globs, never untrusted input. Fixed
# only in brace-expansion 5.0.8, whose named-export shape breaks eslint's
# minimatch 3.x ("expand is not a function"); npm's only alternative is a major
# eslint downgrade — so there is no in-range fix. Accepted 2026-07-28; revisit
# when the eslint/minimatch chain ships a patched brace-expansion in range.
# Mirror of the ALLOWLIST in frontend/scripts/audit-gate.mjs (kept in lockstep).
CVE-2026-14257       # brace-expansion <=5.0.7 unbounded-expansion OOM DoS
GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg  # same advisory — GitHub Advisory DB id Trivy uses for npm
# Follow-up brace-expansion DoS (unbounded intermediate arrays) that bypasses the 5.0.8
# mitigation — same dev-only package + usage, still no in-range fix (any patched version
# breaks eslint's minimatch 3.x, and eslint 9 is peer-capped by eslint-plugin-vue 9.29.0).
# Accepted 2026-08-03; revisit when the eslint/minimatch chain ships a patched range.
GHSA-rgw5-rvv9-x895  # brace-expansion unbounded-intermediate-array DoS (npm audit id)
